   "everything else -> wood"
  ],
  "layering": "on dummies (straw surface) dummy_hit is layered on top of arrow/ball_hit_straw",
  "levels": "ball_hit_* files are densified (tanh soft saturation of the first 30 ms, +4 dB momentary loudness at the same -1 dBFS peak) and arrow_hit_* volume_db sit 2-4 dB lower than in the first set, so with these volume_db values a ball lands ~9 dB louder than an arrow on the same surface (approx. K-weighted momentary loudness; ball stone ~7 dB without the ricochet, ~11-13 dB with it)",
